{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:14.65.380","page_type":"section"},"citation":"14.65.380","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.65.380","content_hash":"11471abce432c1b0494e355aaaff858dd57fe23fd46abac7440df696c5f28231","heading":"Keeping of register.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.65.380:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.65.380","text":"(a) It shall be the duty of the person operating each mobile home park to keep a register containing a record of all mobile home unit owners and tenants located within each park. The register shall contain:\n(1) The name and address of each occupant;\n(2) The make, model, year and manufacturer of each unit;\n(3) The dates of arrival and departure of each unit; and\n(4) The name of the contractors responsible for connections to the utilities.\n(b) The person operating each park shall keep the register available for inspection at all reasonable hours by inspection officers, law enforcement officers, the Director of Environmental Code Services and other officials whose duties necessitate acquisition of the information contained in such register. The original records of the register shall not be destroyed for a period of three years following the date of registration. (Ord. 17074 § 2, 1-28-97. Code 1981 § 25-137. Code 1995 § 98-187.)\nCross References: Police Department, TMC 2.20.090 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"fcbe0037-1c6f-5f27-b49c-fe0625a773db"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.65.380","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.65.380","content_hash":"69c12f82f01230c8e0f2df36f26681f48494c9980ffb3084ec792e0bb9b679f1","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":